(6417148, 950701, 132512, '<td valign="top">Thank you. I thought lying in the gutter would qualify as a unique angle!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LydiaToo:</b></div><hr/><i> I love this! PERFECT for the challenge, too. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thank you. I thought lying in the gutter would qualify as a unique angle! Originally posted by LydiaToo: I love this! PERFECT for the challenge, too. ', '2011-05-18 12:37:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6417161, 950701, 132512, '<td valign="top">Thank you.<br/> <br/>I was lying in the gutter at the bottom of a wall - the wall provided some shade, to help my speedlights compete with the sun.<br/> <br/>Used maximum sync speed of 1/250th at iso 100 to ''kill'' the ambient... hah! all I managed was pale blue.<br/> <br/>two speedlights - one (key light) to the right at 1/4 power (because I was shooting sequences); one to the left at 1/2 power to try to get a rim light - both fired with yongnuo radio triggers.<br/> <br/>many, many, ... many jumps<br/> <br/>default import setting in Lightroom plus I increased contrast and vibrance<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DiscoVader:</b></div><hr/><i> Neat shot, I''d be interested to know how you did it.  Framing is great, love the diagonal, motion blur is just right.  Cool! </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thank you. I was lying in the gutter at the bottom of a wall - the wall provided some shade, to help my speedlights compete with the sun. Used maximum sync speed of 1/250th at iso 100 to ''kill'' the ambient... hah! all I managed was pale blue. two speedlights - one (key light) to the right at 1/4 power (because I was shooting sequences); one to the left at 1/2 power to try to get a rim light - both fired with yongnuo radio triggers. many, many, ... many jumps default import setting in Lightroom plus I increased contrast and vibrance Originally posted by DiscoVader: Neat shot, I''d be interested to know how you did it.  Framing is great, love the diagonal, motion blur is just right.  Cool! ', '2011-05-18 12:51:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6417164, 950701, 132512, '<td valign="top">I wish I was this good at compositing! Just athletes jumping over a wall and global contrast and vibrance adjustments, which I take to be legal as per the Challenge Rules: "You may saturate, desaturate or change the colors of your entry, but no selections are allowed."<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Don''t know how you did this in Basic editing, but great photo, hope it''s legal for your sake. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'I wish I was this good at compositing! Just athletes jumping over a wall and global contrast and vibrance adjustments, which I take to be legal as per the Challenge Rules: "You may saturate, desaturate or change the colors of your entry, but no selections are allowed." Originally posted by Neat: Don''t know how you did this in Basic editing, but great photo, hope it''s legal for your sake. ', '2011-05-18 12:57:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6417166, 950701, 132512, '<td valign="top">Thank you. Since I was using flash and firing sequences I was limited to the maximum flash sync speed of 1/250th. I actually wanted a little bit of blur, for the sense of motion, but agree that fully frozen would have been interesting too.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by supanova:</b></div><hr/><i> Vary good, shame the shutter speed was not faster! </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thank you. Since I was using flash and firing sequences I was limited to the maximum flash sync speed of 1/250th. I actually wanted a little bit of blur, for the sense of motion, but agree that fully frozen would have been interesting too. Originally posted by supanova: Vary good, shame the shutter speed was not faster! ', '2011-05-18 12:59:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(6417169, 950701, 132512, '<td valign="top">It was a lot of fun. These kids were great athletes and they were thrilled that a photographer came out to shoot them.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dali_lama_2k:</b></div><hr/><i> this must have been fun 8 </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'It was a lot of fun. These kids were great athletes and they were thrilled that a photographer came out to shoot them. Originally posted by dali_lama_2k: this must have been fun 8 ', '2011-05-18 13:01:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(6417172, 950701, 132512, '<td valign="top">Thank you. Next time I may try some bigger strobes so I can cut out more of the ambient and freeze the motion. It will be different, not necessarily better...<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vaar:</b></div><hr/><i> Excellent composition! Very original shot! Despite the fact that hand is blurry and even face is not exactly sharp, it is "constructed" so well sharpness becomes only a minor point. Some may say blurriness adds feel of motion. Perhaps :) </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thank you. Next time I may try some bigger strobes so I can cut out more of the ambient and freeze the motion. It will be different, not necessarily better... Originally posted by vaar: Excellent composition! Very original shot! Despite the fact that hand is blurry and even face is not exactly sharp, it is "constructed" so well sharpness becomes only a minor point. Some may say blurriness adds feel of motion. Perhaps :) ', '2011-05-18 13:03:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(6417176, 950701, 132512, '<td valign="top">Me lying in gutter at bottom of a wall looking up.<br/>Kids doing flips over the wall from the other side! Crazy, yes...<br/>Thank you for your vote.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aKiwi:</b></div><hr/><i> What a fantastic photo.!<br/>The point of view is so unique, I still can''t work out what is going on here!<br/>Great composition and lighting.<br/>My pick for a winner. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Me lying in gutter at bottom of a wall looking up.Kids doing flips over the wall from the other side! Crazy, yes...Thank you for your vote. Originally posted by aKiwi: What a fantastic photo.!The point of view is so unique, I still can''t work out what is going on here!Great composition and lighting.My pick for a winner. ', '2011-05-18 13:06:22.000000', NULL, 0),
